---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import heroPhoto from '../../assets/communities/valley-center/valley-center-fall-festival-sunset-hero-crop.jpg';
import recExteriorPhoto from '../../assets/communities/valley-center/valley-center-rec-center-outside-self-owned.JPG';
import valleyPointPhoto from '../../assets/communities/valley-center/valley-center-valley-point-golf-course-sign-no-fence-self-owned.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Valley Center, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A useful introduction to Valley Center, Kansas, with real local imagery and real estate guidance from Charity Menefee."
  pageClass="page-interior page-valley-center"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Valley Center"
    title="Small-town life, with Wichita close by."
    intro="Valley Center has an identity all its own while staying closely connected to the wider Wichita area."
    image={heroPhoto}
    imageAlt="Aerial view of downtown Valley Center at sunset during the Fall Festival, with Main Street leading toward the setting sun"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="0% center"
    imagePositionMobile="43% center"
    imageSizes="(min-width: 48rem) 105rem, 92rem"
    imageWidths={[640, 960, 1280, 1680, 2000]}
    photoCredit="Photo © 2026 Alan Pilcher"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="valley-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left"><p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p><h2 id="valley-overview-title">A Community of Its Own</h2></div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Valley Center sits directly north of Wichita, with Meridian Avenue serving as one of the main north-south routes connecting the city with the surrounding metro.</p>
        <p>What sets Valley Center apart is that it still feels more like a small town than an extension of Wichita. Its established neighborhoods, Main Street area, local events, and smaller scale give the community a distinct identity, while Wichita remains close enough for work, shopping, and other everyday needs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="valley-growth-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Growth and housing</p>
        <h2 id="valley-growth-title">Newer neighborhoods are adding to the housing picture.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Valley Center includes established residential areas while developments such as Amber Ridge, Ceterra, and Arbor Valley show how newer housing has become part of the local picture.</p>
        <p>Those names are reference points, not promises of availability. Compare the individual lot, home condition, neighborhood plans, taxes, and any property-specific HOA or special-assessment details before drawing conclusions about one area from another.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="valley-recreation section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="valley-recreation-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Recreation and local character</p>
          <h2 id="valley-recreation-title">Recreation has a visible place in the community.</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">The Valley Rec Center and Valley Point Golf Course are distinct local reference points, each showing a different side of recreation in Valley Center.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="valley-recreation-feature">
        <div class="valley-recreation-main" data-reveal="left-scale">
          <Picture
            src={recExteriorPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280, 1440]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw"
            alt="The Valley Rec Center building exterior at dusk, with its covered entrance and mural signage"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="valley-recreation-copy" data-reveal="right">
          <p class="eyebrow">A civic landmark</p>
          <h3>The Valley Center Recreation Center</h3>
          <p>Opened in February 2025, the Valley Rec Center is a recent addition to the city's recreation options. The Valley Center Recreation Commission facility on North Meridian Avenue includes a gymnasium, fitness center, indoor track, group exercise studio, and sauna.</p>
          <p>Its aquatics center is built around a six-lane lap pool with a diving board and climbing wall, alongside a zero-depth entry area with a play structure and toddler slide.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="valley-golf-feature">
        <div class="valley-golf-copy" data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Another local reference point</p>
          <h3>Valley Point Golf Course</h3>
          <p>Valley Point Golf Course adds a different visual edge to the community. Its fairways, trees, and pond sit within the broader Valley Center landscape, making the course another recognizable local feature without defining the city as a whole.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="valley-golf-media" data-reveal="right-scale">
          <Picture
            src={valleyPointPhoto}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280, 1600]}
            sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw"
            alt="The Valley Point Golf Course sign beside the course's pond and fairways"
          />
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="valley-fit-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical fit</p>
        <h2 id="valley-fit-title">Compare the setting, not just the address.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Valley Center may be worth a closer look if you're drawn to a quieter small-town environment, want to consider properties with a little more breathing room, or want convenient access to Wichita while living outside the city itself.</p>
        <p>The fit still comes down to the individual property and your normal routines. Compare city-limit boundaries, road access, home type, lot needs, and the places you expect to visit regularly. That keeps the decision grounded in practical details rather than broad assumptions about the community.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="valley-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading"><div data-reveal="left"><p class="eyebrow">Useful questions</p><h2 id="valley-search-title">What should you verify before narrowing the search?</h2></div><p data-reveal="right">The answers can vary by address, especially near city-limit and rural-edge areas. Treat these as starting points for property-specific research.</p></div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Is the property inside Valley Center city limits or near the rural edge, and which services apply to that address?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Which route into Wichita and other regular destinations best fits your normal week?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Are you comparing an established area with a newer neighborhood such as Amber Ridge, Ceterra, or Arbor Valley?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Does the address fall within city utilities, and are any HOA or special-assessment obligations tied to the property?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages"><span>Explore another area</span><a href="/communities/wichita/">Wichita <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a></nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Have questions about Valley Center?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
